This document describes how libicuuc was packaged for build2. In particular,
this understanding will be useful when upgrading to a new upstream
version. See ../README-DEV for general notes on ICU packaging.

Although libicudata does reside in this package, the actual work of
preparing/building the data is done in the icu-tools package, the final
product of which being the ICU data archive file. This package essentially
just converts this data archive into the icudata library.

Symlink the required upstream files into libicu/uc:

$ mkdir -p libicu/uc
$ pushd libicu/uc
$ ln -s ../../../upstream/icu4c/source/common/*.{cpp,h} .
$ mkdir unicode
$ cd unicode
$ ln -s ../../../../upstream/icu4c/source/common/unicode/*.h .
$ popd

We also apply the following patches:

1) Fix the 'unable to find numeric literal operator' MinGW GCC 11 error:

   $ mv libicu/uc/putil.cpp libicu/uc/putil.cpp.orig
   $ cp libicu/uc/putil.cpp.orig libicu/uc/putil.cpp
   $ git apply unable-find-num-literal-op.patch

Note that the above patches are produced by the following commands:

$ git diff ><patch-path>
